# Section 7701 - Definitions

## (a)(1) Person

The term "person" shall be construed to mean and include an individual, a trust, estate, partnership, association, company or corporation.

```catala
declaration enumeration Person:
    -- Individual
    -- Trust
    -- Estate
    -- Partnership content Partnership
    -- Association
    -- Company
    -- Corporation content Corporation
```

## (a)(2) Partnership and partner

The term "partnership" includes a syndicate, group, pool, joint venture, or other unincorporated organization, through or by means of which any business, financial operation, or venture is carried on, and which is not, within the meaning of this title, a trust or estate or a corporation; and the term "partner" includes a member in such a syndicate, group, pool, joint venture, or organization.

```catala
declaration enumeration PartnershipOrganizationForm:
    -- Syndicate
    -- Group
    -- Pool
    -- JointVenture
    -- OtherUnincorporatedOrganization

declaration structure Partnership:
    data form content PartnershipOrganizationForm
    data business_carried_on content boolean
    data is_not_trust_estate_or_corporation content boolean

# Partner: member_of implies membership, no is_member field needed
declaration structure Partner:
    data member_of content Partnership
```

## (a)(3) Corporation

The term "corporation" includes associations, joint-stock companies, and insurance companies.

```catala
declaration enumeration CorporationForm:
    -- Association
    -- JointStockCompany
    -- InsuranceCompany

# determination of domesticity should be separate issue from being
# a corporation or parternership so I remove the fields.
# if any provision needs it it will be determined.
declaration structure Corporation:
    data form content CorporationForm
```

## (a)(4)-(5) Domestic and Foreign

The term "domestic" when applied to a corporation or partnership means created or organized in the United States or under the law of the United States or of any State unless, in the case of a partnership, the Secretary provides otherwise by regulations. 

The term "foreign" when applied to a corporation or partnership means a corporation or partnership which is not domestic.

```catala
declaration enumeration CorpOrPartnership:
    -- Partnership content Partnership
    -- Corporation content Corporation

declaration scope DomesticityDetermination:
    input entity content CorpOrPartnership
    input created_or_organized_in_us_or_under_law content boolean
    context secretary_decision content boolean
    output is_domestic content boolean

scope DomesticityDetermination:
    definition secretary_decision equals false
    label base_rule
    definition is_domestic equals
        created_or_organized_in_us_or_under_law

# if the secretary provides a decision in case of a partnership ship that decision override the base case

  exception base_rule
  definition is_domestic
  under condition
    (match entity with pattern
        -- CorpOrPartnership.Partnership content p : true
        -- CorpOrPartnership.Corporation content c : false)
    and secretary_decision
  consequence equals secretary_decision
```

## (a)(6) Fudiciary

The term "fiduciary" means a guardian, trustee, executor, administrator, receiver, conservator, or any person acting in any fiduciary capacity for any person.

```catala
declaration enumeration FudiciaryForm:
    -- Guardian
    -- Trustee
    -- Executor
    -- Administrator
    -- Receiver
    -- Conservator
    -- Person content Person

declaration structure Fudiciary:
    data fudiciary_type content FudiciaryForm
    data acting_in_any_fudiciary_capacity content boolean
```

## (a)(7) Stock

The term "stock" includes shares in an association, join-stock company, or insurance company

```catala
declaration enumeration ShareHoldingBody:
    -- Association
    -- JointStockCompany
    -- InsuranceCompany

declaration structure Stock:
    data stock_in content ShareHoldingBody
```

## (a)(8) Shareholder

The term "shareholder" includes a member in an association, join-stock company, or insurance company

```catala
declaration enumeration ShareholderMembershipBody:
    -- Association
    -- JointStockCompany
    -- InsuranceCompany

declaration structure Shareholder:
    data shareholding_in content ShareholderMembershipBody
```

## (a)(9)-(10) United States & State
The term "United States" when used in a geographical sense includes only the States and the District of Columbia

The term "State" shall be construded to include the District of Columbia, hwere such construction is necessary to carry out provisions of this title

```catala
# Note that the law does not name the States (IL, CA, NY etc.) so it is open ended term that needs interpretation, but both the definition in 9 and 10 points out to District of Columbia to be include when this provision of the titles are be carried out. One way to formalize this is to just provide a state_id but the law does not says which state or if IL is a state in this definition or CA is a state. For not I provide no code for State

# UnitedStates is just a bare type and though an integer can be used as a field to define United States, it is better understood and interpreted than defined, so no code

```

## (a)(11) Secretary of the Treasury and Secretary

    (A) Secretary of the Treasury
    The term "Secretary of the Treasury" means the Secretary of the Treasury, personally, and shall not include any delegate of his.

    (B) Secretary
    The term "Secretary" means the Secretary of the Treasury or his delegate.

```catala
# Here the law says Secretary  of the Treasury is the person himself there is no other definition, so it is base type and so the a delegate. However the Delegate itself needs determination as to whether the delegate is that of the Secretary or not which is further clarified.

declaration enumeration Secretary:
    -- SecretaryOfTheTreasury
    -- DelegateOfTreasurySecretary content Delegate
```

## (a)(12) Delegate

    (A) In general
        The term "or his delegate"—

        (i) when used with reference to the Secretary of the Treasury, means any officer, employee, or agency of the Treasury Department duly authorized by the Secretary of the Treasury directly, or indirectly by one or more redelegations of authority, to perform the function mentioned or described in the context; and

        (ii) when used with reference to any other official of the United States, shall be similarly construed.

    (B) Performance of certain functions in Guam or American Samoa
    The term "delegate," in relation to the performance of functions in Guam or American Samoa with respect to the taxes imposed by chapters 1, 2, and 21, also includes any officer or employee of any other department or agency of the United States, or of any possession thereof, duly authorized by the Secretary (directly, or indirectly by one or more redelegations of authority) to perform such functions.

---
It is difficult to determine what a delegate constitute because it is an officer that has been assigned to carry out the function. As to how that has been done determination is done is up to the department or the relevant person who redelegates the officer to carry out the function. Then there is a geographic exception or an extension made in case of Guam/American Samoa where one department can designate a delegate from another department. The question about what fields to surface is a judgement, I can surface geography, authorized by etc as boolean and create a scope that satisfies all those conditions, however those are my choices. As such I think Delegate should be base type the determination of which needs to be made based on the interpretation rather than computation.

If we are speaking logically, we can determine certain input variables the knowledge of which can give us some answers, for instance

T  = Referenced official is the Secretary of the Treasury
O  = Referenced official is some other U.S. official
D  = Person is duly authorized (directly OR via redelegation chain)
R  = Authorization comes from the relevant official in context
G  = Function is being performed in Guam or American Samoa
C  = Tax function relates to Chapter 1, 2, or 21
X  = Person belongs to a different dept/agency (outside Treasury)-

IS_DELEGATE_A = (T ∨ O) ∧ D ∧ R
IS_DELEGATE_B = G ∧ C ∧ D ∧ X ∧ R
IS_DELEGATE = IS_DELEGATE_A ∨ IS_DELEGATE_B
---

```catala

declaration scope IsDelegate:
    input is_treasury_or_other_official content boolean
    input is_duly_authorized content boolean
    input authorization_traces_to_official content boolean
    context in_guam_or_samoa content boolean
    context is_chapter_1_2_21 content boolean
    context is_different_dept content boolean
    internal is_delegate_a content boolean
    internal is_delegate_b content boolean
    output determination content boolean

scope IsDelegate:
    definition in_guam_or_samoa equals false
    definition is_chapter_1_2_21 equals false
    definition is_different_dept equals false

    definition is_delegate_a equals (
        is_treasury_or_other_official and 
        is_duly_authorized and 
        authorization_traces_to_official
    )

    definition is_delegate_b equals (
        in_guam_or_samoa and
        is_chapter_1_2_21 and
        is_duly_authorized and
        is_different_dept and
        authorization_traces_to_official
    )

    definition determination equals
        is_delegate_a or is_delegate_b

# I don't know if it is possible or not, but thinking back about is while writing tests scope it is possible to specify the content to be directy another scope so I thought it could be done here as well while defining a structure which forces you to evaluate the function and pass it. However, this will pass the entire function including all its variables - input, internal and output so it is not a full determination. Though one can think of this as match on enum if the field is_delegate inside IsDelegate function is used to check. I don't think this is a good method though. 

# Delegate seems to be determination based on certain facts being true and is determined in a function, however it can also be used as a bare tag in case you just need to match on something. Again, I am not sure this duality is the correct way forward. Just like Domesticity Delegate can just be a condition applied to the said officials, rather than keeping it as a tag. 

# this implies that some definitions can be treated as structures or enums others are just means of determination given some other conditions which I am simply making explicity in the scopes.
declaration structure Delegate:
    data is_delegate content IsDelegate
```

## (a)(13) Commissioner

The term "Commissioner" means the Commissioner of Internal Revenue


```catala
# This is a bare type, a commissioner is a position, that is or isn't. 
# No declaration
```

## (a)(14) Taxpayer

The term "taxpayer" means any person subject to any internal revenue tax.

```catala
# two conditions are specified, one should be a person, and second subjected to tax. The second field is subject to intepretation as nothing has been specified about determination that can be formalized.
# though it raises an interesting question, given these two conditions I can specify a scope for determination, earlier I have just created fields to surface the conditions however, it is possible to provide a single field. Though I don't know how useful that is going to be. This will same as what was done in case of delegate determination. The idea is the structure will carry the information needed for determination as well as the result, serving as determination, however the type as such is a Tag which is not yet determined. So if I specify TaxPayer as a matching field I will have to check the value inside the structure to truly know if that is a tax payer or not, which see wrong and circular. Essentially this makes the structure such as TaxPayer or Delegate an enum rather because it carries the result of being a TaxPayer and hides the true function underneath. 

# Taxpayer is a determination on a person, rather than a type by itself, hence I am removing the declaration.
```

## (a)(15) Military or naval forces and armed forces of the United States

The term "military or naval forces of the United States" and the term "Armed Forces of the United States" each includes all regular and reserve components of the uniformed services which are subject to the jurisdiction of the Secretary of Defense, the Secretary of the Army, the Secretary of the Navy, or the Secretary of the Air Force, and each term also includes the Coast Guard. The members of such forces include commissioned officers and personnel below the grade of commissioned officers in such forces.

```catala
# The decision to make a scope over certain condition depends on whether there is there is an exception or expansion to be made. I favor this view. In the case of (a)(15) the term is used the whole body and the members therein are covered under this blanket term. The determination can be left to interpretation. Here I don't see a need to provide a separate scope. 

# Alternatively one can argue that I can make an enum of jurisdiction and an enum over the jurisdiction and coast guard. But the term is applied over the regular and reserve components which means over the members, which requires interpretation as to who they are and how. Further, the provision applies commissioned officers and personnel below the commissioned officers. So again I can write a scope to express that someone is military if they are part of the jurisdiction or coast guard, they belong to regular or reserved components. But the law goes further to say to close the gap when it mentions the commissioned officers as well though they should have been covered under the term regular components. So significant intepretation is required. Jurisdiction is the best that I can write down, but determination is left to interpretation not calculus in this case.

# This case is beyond my reach, I don't have a clear resolution of this.

declaration enumeration UniformedServicesJurisdiction:
    -- SecretaryOfDefense
    -- SecretaryOfNavy
    -- SecretaryOfAirForce
```

(a)(16) Withholding agent

The term "withholding agent" means any person required to deduct and withhold any tax under the provisions of section 1441, 1442, 1443, or 1461.

```catala
# this is again a determination made on a Person. It assumes there exists a person which who is required to withhold any tax under said provisions. Since the determination is required to be made on Person, I can take Person as an input, however that is no binding on this person as of yet. I can make explicit the conditions under which the determination is made.

declaration scope IsWithholdingAgent:
    input section_id content integer
    internal valid_section_ids content list of integer
    output determination content boolean

scope IsWithholdingAgent:
    definition valid_section_ids equals [1441; 1442; 1443; 1461]
    definition determination equals 
        valid_section_ids contains section_id
```

## (a)(17) Husband and Wife

As used in section 2516, if the husband and wife therein referred to are divorced, wherever appropriate to the meaning of such section, the term "wife" shall be read "former wife" and the term "husband" shall be read "former husband"; and, if the payments described in such section are made by or on behalf of the wife or former wife to the husband or former husband instead of vice versa, wherever appropriate to the meaning of such section, the term "husband" shall be read "wife" and the term "wife" shall be read "husband."

```catala
# There are two separate points that (a)(17) makes. First one is that when someone is divorced and when appropriate the former spouse shall be treated under the term 'wife' or 'husband'. The second point is whenever appropriate when one partner pays to the other 'husband' and 'wife' can be used interchangably. 
# The best I can do is to clarify the first point as an enum, and create a scope

declaration enumeration Spouse:
    -- CurrentPartner
    -- FormerPartnerUnderSection2516

declaration scope IsHusbandOrWife:
    input spouse_current_or_former content Spouse
    output determination content boolean

# if anything other than given in enumeration is passed Catala will error out, so if everything is okay we just return true

scope IsHusbandOrWife:
    definition determination equals true
```

## (a)(18) International organization

The term "international organization" means a public international organization entitled to enjoy privileges, exemptions, and immunities as an international organization under the International Organizations Immunities Act (22 U.S.C. 288–288f).

```catala
# This is again a bare type, the determination is fully made by some other law. Nothing to formalize. It is an entity brought into existence by the law. Also here the term 'public' need legal interpretation which has nothing to formalize
```

## (a)(19) Domestic building and loan association

The term "domestic building and loan association" means a domestic building and loan association, a domestic savings and loan association, and a Federal savings and loan association—
    (A) which is subject by law to supervision and examination by State or Federal authority having supervision over such associations;
    (B) the business of which consists principally of acquiring the savings of the public and investing in loans; and
    (C) at least 60 percent of the amount of the total assets of which (at the close of the taxable year) consists of—
        (i) cash,
        (ii) obligations of the United States or of a State or political subdivision thereof, and stock or obligations of a corporation which is an instrumentality of the United States or of a State or political subdivision thereof, but not including obligations the interest on which is excludable from gross income under section 103,
        (iii) certificates of deposit in, or obligations of, a corporation organized under a State law which specifically authorizes such corporation to insure the deposits or share accounts of member associations,
        (iv) loans secured by a deposit or share of a member,
        (v) loans (including redeemable ground rents, as defined in section 1055) secured by an interest in real property which is (or, from the proceeds of the loan, will become) residential real property or real property used primarily for church purposes, loans made for the improvement of residential real property or real property used primarily for church purposes, provided that for purposes of this clause, residential real property shall include single or multifamily dwellings, facilities in residential developments dedicated to public use or property used on a nonprofit basis for residents, and mobile homes not used on a transient basis,
        (vi) loans secured by an interest in real property located within an urban renewal area to be developed for predominantly residential use under an urban renewal plan approved by the Secretary of Housing and Urban Development under part A or part B of title I of the Housing Act of 1949, as amended, or located within any area covered by a program eligible for assistance under section 103 of the Demonstration Cities and Metropolitan Development Act of 1966, as amended, and loans made for the improvement of any such real property,
        (vii) loans secured by an interest in educational, health, or welfare institutions or facilities, including structures designed or used primarily for residential purposes for students, residents, and persons under care, employees, or members of the staff of such institutions or facilities,
        (viii) property acquired through the liquidation of defaulted loans described in clause (v), (vi), or (vii),
        (ix) loans made for the payment of expenses of college or university education or vocational training, in accordance with such regulations as may be prescribed by the Secretary,
        (x) property used by the association in the conduct of the business described in subparagraph (B), and
        (xi) any regular or residual interest in a REMIC, but only in the proportion which the assets of such REMIC consist of property described in any of the preceding clauses of this subparagraph; except that if 95 percent or more of the assets of such REMIC are assets described in clauses (i) through (x), the entire interest in the REMIC shall qualify.

At the election of the taxpayer, the percentage specified in this subparagraph shall be applied on the basis of the average assets outstanding during the taxable year, in lieu of the close of the taxable year, computed under regulations prescribed by the Secretary. For purposes of clause (v), if a multifamily structure securing a loan is used in part for nonresidential purposes, the entire loan is deemed a residential real property loan if the planned residential use exceeds 80 percent of the property's planned use (determined as of the time the loan is made). For purposes of clause (v), loans made to finance the acquisition or development of land shall be deemed to be loans secured by an interest in residential real property if, under regulations prescribed by the Secretary, there is reasonable assurance that the property will become residential real property within a period of 3 years from the date of acquisition of such land; but this sentence shall not apply for any taxable year unless, within such 3-year period, such land becomes residential real property. For purposes of determining whether any interest in a REMIC qualifies under clause (xi), any regular interest in another REMIC held by such REMIC shall be treated as a loan described in a preceding clause under principles similar to the principles of clause (xi); except that, if such REMIC's are part of a tiered structure, they shall be treated as 1 REMIC for purposes of clause (xi).

```catala
declaration enumeration BuildingAndLoanType:
    -- DomesticBuildingAndLoan
    -- DomesticSavingsAndLoan
    -- FederalSavingsAndLoan

declaration structure Cash:
    data amount content money

declaration structure GovernmentObligations:
    data amount content money
    data is_excludable_under_section_103 content boolean

declaration structure StateInsuredDeposits:
    data amount content money

declaration structure MemberSecuredLoans:
    data amount content money

declaration structure ResidentialRealPropertyLoan:
    data amount content money
    data has_nonresidential_use content boolean
    data planned_residential_use_percent content decimal
    data reasonable_assurance_within_3_years content boolean
    data land_became_residential_within_3_years content boolean

declaration structure UrbanRenewalRealPropertyLoans:
    data amount content money

declaration structure EducationalHealthWelfareLoans:
    data amount content money

declaration structure LiquidatedDefaultProperty:
    data amount content money

declaration structure EducationExpenseLoans:
    data amount content money

declaration structure BusinessUseProperty:
    data amount content money

declaration structure RemicInterest:
    data amount content money
    data qualifying_asset_proportion content decimal

declaration enumeration Asset:
    -- Cash content Cash
    -- GovernmentObligations content GovernmentObligations
    -- StateInsuredDeposits content StateInsuredDeposits
    -- MemberSecuredLoans content MemberSecuredLoans
    -- ResidentialRealPropertyLoan content ResidentialRealPropertyLoan
    -- UrbanRenewalRealPropertyLoans content UrbanRenewalRealPropertyLoans
    -- EducationalHealthWelfareLoans content EducationalHealthWelfareLoans
    -- LiquidatedDefaultProperty content LiquidatedDefaultProperty
    -- EducationExpenseLoans content EducationExpenseLoans
    -- BusinessUseProperty content BusinessUseProperty
    -- RemicInterest content RemicInterest

declaration scope ClassifyGovernmentObligations:
    input go content GovernmentObligations
    output qualifying_amount content money

scope ClassifyGovernmentObligations:
    definition qualifying_amount equals
        if go.is_excludable_under_section_103 then $ 0 else go.amount

declaration scope ClassifyResidentialRealPropertyLoan:
    input rpl content ResidentialRealPropertyLoan
    output qualifying_amount content money

scope ClassifyResidentialRealPropertyLoan:
    definition qualifying_amount equals
        if (not rpl.has_nonresidential_use)
           or rpl.planned_residential_use_percent > 80%
           or (rpl.reasonable_assurance_within_3_years
               and rpl.land_became_residential_within_3_years)
        then rpl.amount else $ 0

declaration scope ClassifyRemicInterest:
    input ri content RemicInterest
    output qualifying_amount content money

scope ClassifyRemicInterest:
    definition qualifying_amount equals
        ri.amount * ri.qualifying_asset_proportion

declaration scope GetAssetAmount:
    input asset content Asset
    output amount content money

scope GetAssetAmount:
    definition amount equals
        match asset with pattern
            -- GovernmentObligations content go :
                (output of ClassifyGovernmentObligations
                    with { -- go: go }).qualifying_amount
            -- ResidentialRealPropertyLoan content rpl :
                (output of ClassifyResidentialRealPropertyLoan
                    with { -- rpl: rpl }).qualifying_amount
            -- RemicInterest content ri :
                (output of ClassifyRemicInterest
                    with { -- ri: ri }).qualifying_amount
            -- Cash content c : c.amount
            -- StateInsuredDeposits content sd : sd.amount
            -- MemberSecuredLoans content ms : ms.amount
            -- UrbanRenewalRealPropertyLoans content urban : urban.amount
            -- EducationalHealthWelfareLoans content ehw : ehw.amount
            -- LiquidatedDefaultProperty content ldp : ldp.amount
            -- EducationExpenseLoans content eel : eel.amount
            -- BusinessUseProperty content bup : bup.amount

declaration scope DetermineDomesticBuildingAndLoan:
    input association_type content BuildingAndLoanType
    input subject_to_supervision content boolean
    input business_is_savings_and_loans content boolean
    input total_assets content money
    input assets content list of Asset
    context election_to_use_average content boolean
    context average_assets_percent content decimal
    internal qualifying_assets content money
    internal qualifying_assets_percent content decimal
    internal effective_percent content decimal
    output is_domestic_building_and_loan content boolean

scope DetermineDomesticBuildingAndLoan:
    definition election_to_use_average equals false
    definition average_assets_percent equals 0%

    definition qualifying_assets equals
        Money.sum of
            (map each asset among assets to
                (output of GetAssetAmount with { -- asset: asset }).amount)

    definition qualifying_assets_percent equals
        qualifying_assets / total_assets * 100%

    label base_assets
    definition effective_percent equals qualifying_assets_percent

    exception base_assets
    definition effective_percent
        under condition election_to_use_average
        consequence equals average_assets_percent

    definition is_domestic_building_and_loan equals
        subject_to_supervision
        and business_is_savings_and_loans
        and effective_percent >= 60%
```
